  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable workbench includes illustrative distance-window review: inspect exact sampled-history interval bounds, boundary censoring and replay positions while retaining archived ISS/SGP4 evidence and downloadable reports.",
  "rationale": "The existing civilian historical replay and fictional multi-object tracks remain the purpose. The actual extracted UI is checked against an analytic relative-distance oracle and exact JSON export, with collision probabilities explicitly absent. POSIX-safe archives and newly complete CPython/PyInstaller notices improve distribution without adding operational prediction or guidance.",
  "limitations": [
    "Historical ISS data and fictional sampled tracks; no live catalog, covariance, collision probability, targeting or maneuver guidance.",
    "Distances are illustrative display thresholds rather than operational safety radii.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
  ],
